  "note": "The basics of the side-view fight (FightGame.basics), one pack for every fighter: crouching, the jump (take-off, up, down, landing), the standing and crouching block poses and their hits, the reactions a character's own game has no clip for (hit while crouching, a low hit, hit in the air, swept, knocked flying, falling down, getting up), the roll (Kyle's dash), the back dash (Mecanim Bot's), the throw pair; and the strikes thrown from a crouch or in the air, the C+D blowback attack (Kyle's launcher) and the throw's grab. Each fighter keeps her own standing A-D strikes, skills, hurt, fall, lying and (if she has one) get-up clips. The 'hit' windows are UFE's active frames (60 per second, after the speed): frame f = f x speed / 60 s of the clip (_work/ufe2/ufe_moves.tsv).",
